        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Work the problem in order: <strong class="text-white">filter, bag, hose, leaks, tank, then the machine itself</strong>. The sixty-second test — hand over the bare inlet port with the hose removed — tells you immediately which half of the system to investigate.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Then prevent the repeat. <strong class="text-white">Fit a collection bag, tap the cartridge between sessions, and empty the tank after every job.</strong> Those three habits keep a shop vac at full strength for a decade or more, because the machine itself has almost nothing in it to wear out.
          </p>
